.el .ds Aq '
.TH sway-things-brightness 1 "" "Sway Things 0.6.0" "Sway Things Manual"
.SH NAME
sway\-things\-brightness \- Print or change the brightness of the screen\*(Aqs backlight, through logind
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsway\-things brightness\fR [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print or change the brightness of the screen\*(Aqs backlight, through logind
.PP
Without \-\-device, the backlight the firmware drives is preferred, as systemd and GNOME prefer it. A backlight never goes below 1 %, so the screen can\*(Aqt go black. External monitors are set on the Brightness & Night Light page (DDC/CI).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
The backlight or keyboard light by its name in /sys/class/backlight or /sys/class/leds, e.g. `intel_backlight` or `tpacpi::kbd_backlight`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Controls when to use color
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
sway\-things\-brightness\-get(1)
Print the brightness in percent
.TP
sway\-things\-brightness\-set(1)
Set the brightness, in percent: 50% or 50
.TP
sway\-things\-brightness\-up(1)
Make it brighter by 5 %
.TP
sway\-things\-brightness\-down(1)
Make it darker by 5 %, not below 1 % for a backlight
